{{ comment }}
{% endif %}

WHAT YOU DO
- Add every keyword from the list as a term, written exactly as in the list. Put it into the existing category whose terms are of the same kind: a database next to databases, a technique next to techniques, a framework next to frameworks, a platform next to platforms. A technique or a discipline never goes into a category of libraries or tools (do not put "multimodal generation" next to PyTorch and Pandas): it goes into the techniques category, or the keyword is skipped. Prefer the closest existing category even when the fit is loose: APIs, SDKs and protocols go to the backend category, libraries to the libraries category. Create a new last line only when the keyword fits no existing category at all (for example a cloud platform when the list has no platform category), and then give it a normal category name of one or two words, never a name that repeats the keywords ("APIs and SDKs"). Use at most one new line.
- Add a keyword only if it reads as a short term in a skills list (a tool, a language, a framework, a library, a technique, a protocol, a platform). A keyword that is a duty, an industry or a way of working (backend engineering, production systems, frontend delivery, stakeholder communication) does not belong in this list: skip it, even though it is in the keyword list.
- Never add a term that is not in the keyword list. Do not add tools or languages from your own knowledge, and do not copy tools from the job posting. Before you answer, check every term you added against the keyword list: a term that is not in the list is removed. Example: the posting names LlamaIndex and Vercel AI SDK, the keyword list does not: they must not appear in your answer.
- Keep the candidate's programming languages and main frameworks and libraries in the list.
- Inside a category put the terms most relevant to the posting first. Keep the category order, the category labels exactly as written, the separators and the line breaks.
- Remove a term only when it is clearly irrelevant to this posting and a keyword of the same kind takes its place in that category. Remove at most 3 terms in total.

OUTPUT RULES
- Return every unit with the same number n and the same type.
- Plain text only: no markdown, no HTML other than the tags shown below.

OUTPUT FORMAT
Only the units, nothing else:

<el n="0">first category: term, term
second category: term, term</el>
